Next.js serves everything in this directory at the site root.

It is empty today — the favicon is generated by app/icon.svg and robots.txt
and sitemap.xml are routes — but the directory itself has to exist, because
the Dockerfile copies it into the runtime image. Git does not store empty
directories, so without this file the directory vanishes on clone and the
image build fails with "/repo/apps/web/public: not found".

The Dockerfile also creates it defensively, so deleting this file is
survivable. Both belts are deliberate: this failure only appears on a clean
clone, which means it appears in production and nowhere else.
